 one mood and misses the other basin. (3) the traces make the freeze visible: flat energy lines vs the quantum arm's jumps between basins. (4) the flip histogram is the mechanism -- classical MH can only flip one spin at a time; the Trotterised proposal flips whole regions. (5) the convergence ladder is the headline: how many steps until the bailout ranking matches the exact answer. (6) regret bars: what picking the wrong bank/street costs at each budget.","caveats":["convergence ladders are prefix-truncated versions of the SAME chains (within-run convergence), not independent restarts","wall-clock cost differs strongly between arms (ms/step reported); the headline is steps-to-correct-ranking, the iteration budget","the recorded quantum arm ran on an unseeded simulator, so numbers vary run-to-run; the reported ranking gaps are far larger than that spread"]}}